# ⚡ Docker Desktop + WSL Quick Start (Requires Admin)

## 1. Prerequisites
- Windows 10 (2004+) or Windows 11  
- Admin rights (required for WSL & Docker Desktop)  
- At least 4GB RAM free  
- Internet connection  

---

## 2. Enable WSL & Virtualization
Run PowerShell **as Administrator**:
```cmd
wsl --install
```
👉 This installs **WSL2** and the default Linux distribution (Ubuntu).  
Verify:
```cmd
wsl --version
```

Enable virtualization in BIOS if not already enabled.

---

## 3. Install Docker Desktop
1. Download from Docker Desktop for Windows [(docker.com in Bing)](https://www.bing.com/search?q="https%3A%2F%2Fwww.docker.com%2Fproducts%2Fdocker-desktop%2F")  
2. Run installer (requires admin)  
3. During setup, select **WSL2 backend**  
4. Restart system if prompted  

---

## 4. Configure WSL Integration
Open Docker Desktop → **Settings → Resources → WSL Integration**  
- Enable integration with your chosen distro (e.g., Ubuntu)  

---

## 5. Verify Installation
```cmd
docker --version
docker run hello-world
```

Inside WSL:
```bash
docker run -it ubuntu bash
```

---

## 6. Useful Commands
```cmd
# List containers
docker ps -a

# List images
docker images

# Remove container
docker rm <container_id>

# Remove image
docker rmi <image_id>

# Stop all containers
docker stop $(docker ps -q)
```

